From 43427aa2184ddd1551f83f223fd85050af10cc64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TekRantGaming <52795608+TekRantGaming@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:54:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] D3D12: let a frame wait briefly for pipelines created in the
 background

async_shader_wait_ms (default 0, so unchanged unless set): with
async_shader_compilation, a draw whose pipeline is still being created
waits for it, within a per-frame budget, instead of being skipped at
once. Pipelines are created on many threads at once, so most finish
within a few milliseconds: no long pause, and few draws go missing.
Pipeline::creation_done tells "still being created" from "failed".

Testing aids (environment variables, no effect otherwise):
REX_DEV_SHADER_SALT adds text to the DXBC generator name so the driver's
shader cache sees every shader as new; REX_DEV_PIPELINE_STATS logs pipeline
waits and skipped draws once a second.
---
